    We finally set the pausible gain gain based on the no-amplified gyro integration of attitude estimation.
    Also note that there are two limitation for the LQI-attitude based control, that is, the limitation of the hydrus.
    1. The yaw control still unstable when some of the propeller become close to the limit(e.g. l-form). We improve the stability by increasing the gain of p and d, and decrease that of i.
    2. The trackability of the attitude is not very good in some special forms(e.g. l-form), this is the limitation of the LQI attitude based position control algorithm.
    We improve, to some of the extent, by increasing the p gain of the roll and pitch, but too much raising results in the vibration of the tilt.
    
    Both problem can be solved by adding tilt-rotor.

